Description: transparent open-source malware detection engine
 CAU is a malware detection and triage engine written in Go. Fourteen
 detectors read every file once; every finding is explained with a labeled
 class and a MITRE ATT&CK technique, and every report is machine-readable
 with CI-friendly exit codes (JSON and SARIF output).
 .
 It scans files and directories, inspects the live process table for fileless,
 masquerade and injection indicators, analyses UEFI firmware images, and
 gates detection changes against a measured evaluation baseline. YARA matching
 is provided through libyara.
 .
 This package ships the "cau" scanner, the "cau-mcp" Model Context Protocol
 server, and the bundled detection content (YARA rules and signature
 databases). Optional systemd units for scheduled and resident scanning are
 installed but not enabled by default.
